-- title:
--   G Comm Stability Scalar
-- statement:
--   **First scalar G-commutativity stability bound.** Let $S$ be a symmetric projective strategy for $(m+1,q,d)$ with normalized state, let $G^x$ be an indexed polynomial submeasurement family for $(m,q,d)$, and let $\zeta$ be an error parameter. Assume the family identity and the `SliceBoundednessInput` with error $\zeta$.
--
--   For each $y\in\mathbb{F}_q$, let $R^y$ be the submeasurement obtained by uniformly averaging the evaluated point-family sandwich around the slice measurement $G^y$, let $T_y$ be the total operator of $G^y$, and let $W_{y,g}$ be the averaged slice point-evaluation operator. Define
--
--   $$
--   \Delta_1(y)=\sum_g\operatorname{ev}_\psi\!\left(\operatorname{leftTensor}(R^y_g(1-T_y))\,\operatorname{rightTensor}(W_{y,g})\right).
--   $$
--
--   Then the uniform average of this defect obeys
--
--   $$
--   \left|\mathbb E_{y\sim\operatorname{Unif}(\mathbb{F}_q)}\Delta_1(y)\right|\le\sqrt{\zeta}.
--   $$
--
--   This is the first scalar stability estimate in the evaluated-slice commutativity chain.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Commutativity.gCommStability_scalar`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/Commutativity/GCommStability/Scalar/First.lean#L61-L108

